@startuml implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - states of an implementation issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub. Each arrow names one row of issue-states.md (I1 to I12); I9 and I11 are notes.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft\n(no status label)" as Draft
state "cumin/status/ready" as Ready
state "cumin/status/implementing" as Implementing
state "cumin/status/awaiting-checks" as Checks
state "cumin/status/reviewing" as Reviewing
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review" as OwnerReview
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft : Planner or Owner creates\na sub-issue
Draft --> Ready : Owner checks it,\nadds cumin/status/ready
Ready --> Implementing : I1 cumin asks for the implementation
Implementing --> Checks : I2 run done,\npull request verified
Implementing --> Decision : I2 blocked, or\ntwo abnormal ends
Checks --> Reviewing : I3 required checks passed
Checks --> Implementing : I4 a required check failed,\nfix request
Checks --> Decision : I4 fix requests\nat the limit
Reviewing --> Implementing : I5 REQUEST_CHANGES\n(fix request)
Reviewing --> [*] : I6 APPROVE, risk/low\n(cumin merges)
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : I7 APPROVE,\nrisk/medium or risk/high
Reviewing --> Decision : I8 comments left\nafter 3 rounds
Reviewing --> Decision : I10 Reviewer\nreturned blocked
OwnerReview --> [*] : I12 Owner approves the head commit\n(cumin merges)
OwnerReview --> Ready : Owner sends it back\n(comment, cumin/status/ready again)
Decision --> Ready : Owner answers,\nadds cumin/status/ready again

note "I11: in every state, cumin copies the\ncumin/status/* and risk/* labels of the\nissue to its open pull request." as I11
note "I9: after every merge (I6, I12, or by the Owner),\ncumin copies the work left to a follow-up note." as I9

@enduml
